-- Sous — catalog expansion: +100 recipes, 58 -> 158.
--
-- WHY THIS SHAPE. The starter catalog was one family's rotation: 52 of its 58
-- dishes were Mexican, Asian or Italian, and only 6 were vegan against a
-- 28-day reuse window — so a plant-based household got one full week and then
-- a shrinking one. This fills both gaps: ~35 of the 100 are vegetarian or
-- vegan, and the rest spread across Indian, Middle Eastern, Mediterranean,
-- Thai, Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese, Chinese, American, French, Spanish,
-- Caribbean, African and Eastern European.
--
-- TAGGING IS SAFETY-CRITICAL. candidate_recipes fails closed: a recipe with no
-- dietary_tags is treated as unclassified and never offered to a household with
-- any restriction. Every recipe below carries tags, and every new ingredient
-- carries its allergens, because the filter cross-checks both.
--
-- One trap worth naming: contains_pork / contains_beef / contains_poultry have
-- NO backing allergen token, so the derivation at the bottom cannot infer them
-- from ingredients the way it infers contains_dairy or contains_nuts. They are
-- set explicitly on every meat dish here, and the final block additionally
-- strips vegetarian/vegan from anything carrying a meat tag — so a future
-- mis-tag fails safe instead of serving chicken to a vegetarian.
--
-- Idempotent: guarded inserts throughout, safe to re-run.

-- ===========================================================================
-- SECTION 1 — Indian (12) + Middle Eastern (10)
-- ===========================================================================

